plain
Array → json_encode → xor_encrypt → base64_encode → Cookie
The Attack
Table
Property	Value
Known plaintext	{"showpassword":"no","bgcolor":"#ffffff"}
Your cookie	EGAgHwQ1IxYYMSQYGSZxTUksPFVHYDEQCC0/GBlgaVVIJDURDSQ1VRY=
Recovered key	kBSw
XOR property: plaintext ^ ciphertext = key
Python Exploit
Python
import base64
import json

# Your cookie
cookie = "EGAgHwQ1IxYYMSQYGSZxTUksPFVHYDEQCC0/GBlgaVVIJDURDSQ1VRY="

# Known plaintext
plaintext = b'{"showpassword":"no","bgcolor":"#ffffff"}'

# Recover key
cipher = base64.b64decode(cookie)
key = bytes([p ^ c for p, c in zip(plaintext, cipher)])
# Key: kBSw

# Forge new cookie
new_plain = json.dumps({"showpassword":"yes", "bgcolor":"#ffffff"})
new_cipher = bytes([ord(new_plain[i]) ^ key[i % len(key)] for i in range(len(new_plain))])
new_cookie = base64.b64encode(new_cipher).decode()
